<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 12 June, from 910 to 1987.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/910">910 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,116 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Magyars defeat King Louis the Child's army near Augsburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> army defeated the combined forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a>, under the nominal command of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-child">Louis the Child</a>, on the Lechfeld south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a>, using the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feigned-retreat">feigned retreat</a>. The victors broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> for the first time.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-child">Louis the Child</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1240">1240 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">786 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Disputation of Paris opens at the court of Louis IX</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the court of King Louis IX, four rabbis defended the Talmud against the charges of blasphemy pressed by Nicholas Donin, a Jewish convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. The disputation led to a decree for the public burning of all available Talmud <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1418">1418 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">608 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Paris mob kills Bernard VII of Armagnac and his supporters</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> during the civil war, a mob killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-vii-count-of-armagnac">Bernard VII, Count of Armagnac</a> and constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, together with his sympathisers, all prisoners, foreign bankers, and students and faculty of the College of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-vii-count-of-armagnac">Bernard VII of Armagnac</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1429">1429 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">597 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc leads the French to capture Jargeau</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the second day of the Battle of Jargeau, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> led the French army in taking the city and capturing the English commander, William de la Pole, 1st Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suffolk">Suffolk</a>. It was her first offensive battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1665">1665 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">361 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New York is incorporated as an English city</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nicolls">Richard Nicolls</a> replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> government with an English mayor, aldermen and sheriff. The English had taken the colony from the Dutch the previous year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/virginia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virginia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Virginia adopts its Declaration of Rights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Drafted mainly by George Mason, the Declaration set out rights such as freedom of the press and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jury-trial">trial by jury</a>. It influenced the US Bill of Rights and the French Declaration of 1789.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1898">1898 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emilio Aguinaldo declares Philippine independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kawit">Kawit</a>, Cavite, revolutionaries proclaimed independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> annexed the islands instead, and full independence came only in 1946.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nelson Mandela is sentenced to life imprisonment</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mandela and seven co-accused in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rivonia-trial">Rivonia Trial</a> were sentenced to life for sabotage. He spent 27 years in prison before his release in 1990.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1987">1987 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">39 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Reagan urges Gorbachev to 'tear down this wall'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> Gate, President Reagan challenged the Soviet leader to open the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a>. It fell two and a half years later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 12 June <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozong-of-song"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-gaozong-of-song.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Gaozong of Song</span><span class="tp">1107–1187</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cosimo-i-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cosimo I de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1519–1574</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/harry-johnston"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/harry-johnston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Harry Johnston</span><span class="tp">1858–1927</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-frank"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anne-frank.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anne Frank</span><span class="tp">1929–1945</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 12 June <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aethelflaed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Æthelflæd</span><span class="tp">c. 870–918</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bernard-vii-count-of-armagnac"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bernard-vii-count-of-armagnac.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bernard VII, Count of Armagnac</span><span class="tp">c. 1360–1418</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-iii-gonzaga"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludovico-iii-gonzaga.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludovico III Gonzaga</span><span class="tp">1412–1478</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez-de-cuellar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-velazquez-de-cuellar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar</span><span class="tp">1465–1524</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-yoshimoto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/imagawa-yoshimoto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Imagawa Yoshimoto</span><span class="tp">1519–1560</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-ii-duke-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-emmanuel-ii-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles Emmanuel II, Duke of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1634–1675</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-fitzjames-1st-duke-of-berwick"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-fitzjames-1st-duke-of-berwick.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James FitzJames, 1st Duke of Berwick</span><span class="tp">1670–1734</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-tukhachevsky"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikhail-tukhachevsky.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mikhail Tukhachevsky</span><span class="tp">1893–1937</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
